 "lines": [
  {
   "text": "In 1518, a woman in Strasbourg started dancing and couldn't stop.",
   "s": 0.12,
   "e": 4.058
  },
  {
   "text": "Frau Troffea danced in the street for almost a week.",
   "s": 4.358,
   "e": 6.981
  },
  {
   "text": "Then her neighbors joined in. Soon, thirty-four people were dancing.",
   "s": 7.281,
   "e": 10.736
  },
  {
   "text": "Within a month, there were about four hundred.",
   "s": 11.036,
   "e": 12.866
  },
  {
   "text": "So the doctors made their diagnosis: \"hot blood.\"",
   "s": 13.166,
   "e": 15.907
  },
  {
   "text": "Their cure? Even more dancing.",
   "s": 16.087,
   "e": 17.453
  },
  {
   "text": "The city cleared out halls, built a wooden stage, and hired musicians.",
   "s": 17.753,
   "e": 21.22
  },
  {
   "text": "But the music only pulled in more dancers.",
   "s": 21.52,
   "e": 23.626
  },
  {
   "text": "So the city did the opposite. It banned music, and dancing.",
   "s": 23.926,
   "e": 26.781
  }
 ],
